        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Romania’s pro-EU coalition collapse 'does not alter the country's foreign policy', analyst says Europe Issued on: 05/05/2026 - 20:33 Modified: 05/05/2026 - 20:34 Romania's parliament on Tuesday voted to oust liberal Prime Minister Ilie Bolojan in a motion of no confidence initiated by the Social Democrats and the far right, deepening political turmoil in the EU and NATO country bordering Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Laurențiu Pleșca, Policy Fellow at the German Marshall Fund of the United States. He says that the collapse of the government \"does not alter Romania's foreign policy or security trajectory\". Putin ‘doesn’t care' about Russians or Ukrainians: ‘Pageantry and symbolism’ over civilian lives 05/05/2026 Europe Two dead as car ploughs into crowd in Germany's Leipzig 04/05/2026 Europe Europe, Canada pull together in Yerevan in Trump's shadow 04/05/2026 Europe ‘Far beyond’ EU and NATO: Armenia hosts EPC summit cast as ‘gateway’ in shifting diplomatic order 04/05/2026 Europe New tariff hike could cost Germany $18BN 02/05/2026 Germany Berlin urges stronger European defence 02/05/2026 Germany The industrial crisis is challenging both the EU and France's distinct social and economic models 01/05/2026 France Macron on the world stage: French president 'very popular everywhere in Europe, except for France' 01/05/2026 France Germany says 'prepared' for any US troop reduction 30/04/2026 Europe"
